  "provenance": "Every `rules` value was GENERATED by running the authority (parseRedirectsCsv then resolveRedirects) over the `csv` above it on 2026-08-26, not written by hand. The hand-written first draft got the hop-cap case wrong and both implementations agreed against it, which is the reason this line exists.",
  "reportFields": "`rules` is what serves. `loops`, `duplicates` and `flattened` are the REPORT, and they are in the fixture because they are what the operator is TOLD: a cycle and an over-cap chain both serve nothing, so asserting only `rules` cannot tell the two apart. Removing cycle detection from one implementation left every `rules` value identical, which is how this half of the fixture came to exist."
